+    ///
+    /// A port that is not written is `80`: this client speaks `http` and nothing else, so the
+    /// default is the scheme's. `https` is refused with the reason rather than attempted
+    /// (`Class`'s sibling decision above).
+    ///
+    /// # Errors
+    ///
+    /// [`Error::Invalid`] when the endpoint is not an authority this client can speak to, and
+    /// [`Error::Transport`] when the runtime itself cannot be built.
