+/// What one pass did, as counts.
+///
+/// One type for both passes because they answer one question each and a script reads them the same
+/// way: `moved`/`bytes` are what [`sweep`] took out of the box, `fetched`/`bytes` are what
+/// [`hydrate`] brought back, and `kept` is what a pass looked at and left where it was (a warm
+/// segment, or one whose local file was already the length the manifest states). Every count is
+/// what the *manifest* says rather than what a directory happens to hold: the manifest is the store
+/// (`lakelet/4.8-compaction`), and a report a reader can check against it is a report that can be
+/// wrong out loud.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct Report {
+    /// Segments this pass took out of the box.
+    moved: u64,
+    /// Segments this pass brought back into it.
+    fetched: u64,
+    /// Segments this pass looked at and left alone.
+    kept: u64,
+    /// Bytes these segments weigh, as the manifest states them.
+    bytes: u64,
+    /// Pages of listing this pass read.
+    pages: u64,
+}
